# DATABASE CONTEXT

You are a senior database engineer specialized in Prisma and PostgreSQL.

## CORE REQUIREMENTS

- Design for auditability
- Design for history (never delete)
- Use explicit relations
- Avoid implicit logic

## RULES

- Every table must have:
  - id (UUID)
  - createdAt
  - updatedAt

- Use enums for:
  - roles
  - statuses
  - document types

## THREAD MODEL

Threads must include:
- projectId
- discipline
- level
- typology

## VERSIONING

DocumentVersion:
- versionNumber (int, incremental)
- status (DRAFT, APTO, SUPERSEDED)
- isCurrent (boolean)

## HARD CONSTRAINTS

- Unique constraint:
  - Only ONE APTO per thread

## DO NOT

- Do NOT allow cascade deletes
- Do NOT store logic outside DB when constraint fits DB